1. A fuel cell control device for controlling operation of a fuel cell system including a fuel cell stack, an anode gas supply path, and an anode gas circulation path configured to circulate anode off-gas discharged from an anode of the fuel cell stack back to the anode, the fuel cell control device comprising:

an anode gas circulation flow rate control unit configured to control a circulation flow rate of an anode gas flowing through the anode gas circulation path;

a wet/dry state detecting unit configured to detect or estimate a wet/dry state of the fuel cell stack;

a priority setting unit configured to set, based on the wet/dry state detected or estimated by the wet/dry state detecting unit, a control priority between a wet-state suppressing control for reducing excessive wetness in the fuel cell stack and a dry-state suppressing control for reducing drying of the fuel cell stack;

a limiting unit configured to set a limit value for the circulation flow rate of the anode gas according to the control priority set by the priority setting unit; and

a compensation unit configured to compensate a target circulation flow rate determined for the anode gas circulation flow rate control unit based on the limit value set by the limiting unit,

wherein the anode gas circulation flow rate control unit controls the circulation flow rate of the anode gas in accordance with the compensated target circulation flow rate such that, when the wet-state suppressing control has priority, accumulation of liquid water in the fuel cell stack is suppressed, and, when the dry-state suppressing control has priority, drying of an electrolyte membrane of the fuel cell stack is suppressed.
